+# Deterministic retraction sampling. The original version of this test assumed
+# OpenAlex relevance ordering would rank the retracted original first; the
+# 2026-11-24 live run disproved that assumption — the top relevance hit was a
+# genuinely non-retracted 'Faculty Opinions recommendation' peer-review
+# commentary (W4213234079), and the test failed on its is_retracted assertion.
+# The rewrite keeps the exact same query and only appends the deterministic
+# is_retracted:true filter for the retracted scenario, so the sample is the
+# API's retraction signal, not ranking luck. The commentary itself is covered
+# by test_retraction_commentary_type_policy_offline below: its pool exclusion
+# is the peer-review type policy, never a retraction judgement.
+RETRACTED_FILTER_FRAGMENT = ',is_retracted:true'
 
